{%- comment -%}
  PERSONALIZATION FLOWS
  =====================

  Two kinds of visitor reach the product page, and they should not see the
  same page:

    quiz    — arrived via the landing page and completed the customization
              quiz, so they already know their formula and have already seen
              some of the story.
    direct  — landed on the product page cold. Generic wording, full story.

  Shopify caches pages for everyone, so this cannot be decided in Liquid —
  Liquid never sees the visitor's cookies. Instead every variant is rendered
  into the page and the browser picks one. This script runs in <head>, before
  anything paints, and stamps the answer on <html>:

    data-ll-flow      quiz | direct
    data-ll-strength  strong | medium | sensitive

  component-flow.css then shows the matching copy and hides sections that do
  not belong to the active flow. Because the choice is made by CSS on an
  attribute that is set before first paint, there is no flash of the wrong
  version.

  HOW A VISITOR BECOMES "quiz"
  ----------------------------
  The quiz writes ll_flow=quiz when it hands off to the product page
  (assets/quiz.js, assets/quiz_2.js). The strength cookie on its own is NOT
  enough: the product page's own strength picker writes one too, so a direct
  visitor who clicks around would otherwise be misread as a quiz arrival.

  Visitors who took the quiz before ll_flow existed are still recognised, by
  the starting_shade cookie — only the two quizzes ever write that.

  SWITCHING FLOWS FOR TESTING
  ---------------------------
  Add to any URL:

    ?ll_flow=quiz&ll_strength=sensitive   pose as a quiz arrival
    ?ll_flow=direct                       pose as a cold arrival
    ?ll_flow=auto                         stop posing, go back to the truth
    ?ll_reset=1                           become a brand new visitor

  These are sticky: the parameter rewrites the cookie, so the chosen flow
  survives clicking through to other pages instead of lasting one page view.
  That is the point — a flow is a journey across several pages, and testing it
  one URL at a time would not tell you much. It means a quiz taker can flip
  themselves to the direct version and browse it as if they had landed cold,
  and back again.

  ll_strength rewrites the strength cookie proper, the same one the quiz
  writes, so the rest of the product page (variant selection, ingredient copy)
  follows along rather than only the wording this file governs.

  ?ll_flow=auto clears only the forced flow and returns to normal detection: a
  past quiz taker goes back to being a quiz arrival, everyone else to direct.
  ('reset' is accepted as a spelling of this too.)

  ?ll_reset=1 goes further and clears everything the quiz wrote — flow,
  strength, shades, name — so the next page load looks like a first ever visit.
  This is the state worth testing most and the hardest to reach by hand.

  Because it is sticky, do not put these parameters in a link you publish —
  anyone who clicks it is switched for real. They are a testing tool.

  In the theme editor nothing is ever hidden unless a flow is named in the URL
  this way — otherwise half the page would vanish from the editor and look
  broken.
{%- endcomment -%}
<script>
  (function () {
    var root = document.documentElement;

    function cookie(name) {
      var m = document.cookie.match('(?:^|;\\s*)' + name + '=([^;]*)');
      return m ? decodeURIComponent(m[1]) : '';
    }

    function param(name) {
      var m = window.location.search.match('[?&]' + name + '=([^&]*)');
      return m ? decodeURIComponent(m[1]) : '';
    }

    var FOREVER = '; expires=Fri, 31 Dec 9999 23:59:59 GMT; path=/;';

    function write(name, value) {
      document.cookie = name + '=' + value + FOREVER;
    }

    function clear(name) {
      document.cookie = name + '=; expires=Thu, 01 Jan 1970 00:00:01 GMT; path=/;';
    }

    var flowParam = param('ll_flow');
    var strengthParam = param('ll_strength');

    // ?ll_reset=1 — become a brand new visitor. Everything the quiz leaves
    // behind is cleared, which is the one state a tester cannot otherwise get
    // back to without emptying the browser by hand.
    if (param('ll_reset')) {
      ['ll_flow', 'strength', 'starting_shade', 'ending_shade', 'firstname', 'lastname'].forEach(clear);
      flowParam = '';
      strengthParam = '';
    }

    // The testing parameters rewrite the cookies rather than applying for one
    // page view, so the chosen flow carries across the whole journey.
    // 'auto' only drops the forced flow, leaving the quiz's own answers in
    // place, so a real quiz taker goes back to being one.
    if (flowParam === 'auto' || flowParam === 'reset') {
      clear('ll_flow');
      flowParam = '';
    } else if (flowParam === 'quiz' || flowParam === 'direct') {
      write('ll_flow', flowParam);
    }

    if (strengthParam === 'strong' || strengthParam === 'medium' || strengthParam === 'sensitive') {
      write('strength', strengthParam);
    }

    var flow = flowParam || cookie('ll_flow');

    // Legacy quiz takers predate the ll_flow cookie; starting_shade is written
    // by the quizzes and nothing else. An explicit ll_flow cookie wins over
    // this, which is what lets ?ll_flow=direct stick for someone who has in
    // fact taken the quiz.
    if (!flow && cookie('starting_shade')) {
      flow = 'quiz';
    }

    var strength = strengthParam || cookie('strength');
    if (strength === 'gentle') {
      strength = 'sensitive';
    }
    if (strength !== 'strong' && strength !== 'medium' && strength !== 'sensitive') {
      strength = 'medium';
    }

    root.setAttribute('data-ll-flow', flow === 'quiz' ? 'quiz' : 'direct');
    root.setAttribute('data-ll-strength', strength);

    // In the editor, show every section regardless of flow unless the URL
    // explicitly asks for one, so the merchant can still see and click
    // everything they have placed.
    if (window.Shopify && window.Shopify.designMode && !flowParam) {
      root.setAttribute('data-ll-editor', 'true');
    }
  })();
</script>
